al in Sydney, and Respironics began selling a commercial adult device in 1985. [1]","It is described as the most effective treatment for moderate to severe obstructive sleep apnea and, in people with sleep apnea, lowers overall risk of cardiovascular death. [1] Case series have reported reduced seizure frequency in people with epilepsy and sleep apnea who used CPAP. [2]","Looksmaxxing communities discuss CPAP for facial puffiness and appearance; no appearance studies were found."],"infobox":[["Type","Medical device"],["Developed","1980 (adult CPAP, Colin Sullivan)"],["First commercial adult device","1985 (Respironics)"],["Mask types","Nasal, full-face, nasal pillows, hybrid"],["Status","Prescribed"]],"sections":[{"h":"Effectiveness and adherence","paras":["CPAP eliminates obstructive apneas in most people who use it as recommended. [1] Adherence is a major problem: about 8% quit after the first night and more than half within the first year. [1] A small series of refractory epilepsy patients with sleep apnea found that success depended largely on compliance. [2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Adverse effects","paras":["Users may report discomfort, nasal congestion, bloating, claustrophobia, mask leaks and mouth leaks. [1] Full-face masks and chin straps are used to manage mouth leaks. [1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["A 1994 case series of seven patients with refractory partial epilepsy and sleep apnea reported reduced seizure frequency in six after treating apnea, including four of five with CPAP. [2] No studies found examining CPAP for facial puffiness or appearance."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1980","event":"Colin Sullivan builds an adult CPAP machine in Sydney. [1]"},{"year":"1985","event":"Respironics sells one of the first commercial adult CPAP machines. [1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Continuous positive airway pressure","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continuous_positive_airway_pressure","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Epilepsy and sleep apnea syndrome","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7969960/","source":"Neurology","year":1994,"type":"study"}],"studies":[{"title":"Epilepsy and sleep apnea syndrome","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7969960/","source":"Neurology","year":1994,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"how do you larp sleep apnea?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-do-you-larp-sleep-apnea.1927848/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260330112719/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-do-you-larp-sleep-apnea.1927848/"},{"title":"Dude got Bimax for sleep apnea, got chimpmaxxed and no breathing improvement","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/dude-got-bimax-for-sleep-apnea-got-chimpmaxxed-and-no-breathing-improvement.1767003/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251217073845/https://looksmax.org/threads/dude-got-bimax-for-sleep-apnea-got-chimpmaxxed-and-no-breathing-improvement.1767003/"},{"title":"fake sleep apnea guide","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/fake-sleep-apnea-guide.1759987/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260101121456/https://looksmax.org/threads/fake-sleep-apnea-guide.1759987/"},{"title":"lower jaw surgery sleep apnea","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/lower-jaw-surgery-sleep-apnea.1682828/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251215121358/https://looksmax.org/threads/lower-jaw-surgery-sleep-apnea.1682828/"},{"title":"what the fuck do i do when i have diagnosed severe sleep apnea","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/what-the-fuck-do-i-do-when-i-have-diagnosed-severe-sleep-apnea.1483265/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250812015210/https://looksmax.org/threads/what-the-fuck-do-i-do-when-i-have-diagnosed-severe-sleep-apnea.1483265/"},{"title":"what else can i do to make my moderate sleep apnea because of my recessed chin appear worse at the sleep study","url":"https://looksm